            ["**Interrupting**", "Normal and friendly in Italy, Brazil and much of the Middle East; rude in Japan, Finland and Indonesia"],
            ["**Saying** *no*", "Direct refusal is fine in Germany and the Netherlands. In much of Asia, *that would be difficult* or a change of subject *is* the no"],
            ["**Disagreeing with seniors publicly**", "Expected in Sweden and the Netherlands; can be genuinely career-limiting elsewhere. Where it is, the private one-to-one before the meeting is how it is done"],
            ["**Small talk before business**", "Skipped in Germany and the Netherlands; essential in Brazil, India, the Middle East and much of Latin America"],
            ["**Deadlines**", "Treated as fixed commitments in Germany, Japan and Switzerland; as intentions to be renegotiated in some other business cultures"],
            ["**First names**", "Immediate in the US, UK, Australia and Nordics; titles matter far more in Germany, Japan, Korea and much of Latin Europe"],
            ["**Written follow-up**", "In high-context cultures, a written summary after a verbal agreement can read as distrust. Frame it as *notes for my own record*"]
